==Taxonomy==
The genus ''Cyclamen'' was first described by [[Carl Linnaeus]] in ''[[Species Plantarum]]'' in 1753.<ref name="IPNI_32774-1">{{cite web |title=''Cyclamen'' L. |work=[[International Plant Names Index|The International Plant Names Index]] |url=https://www.ipni.org/n/32774-1 |access-date=2021-05-08 }}</ref> It was traditionally classified in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Primulaceae]], was reclassified in the family Myrsinaceae<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.britannica.com/plant/Cyclamen|title=''Cyclamen'' |website=Encyclopedia Britannica|access-date=2019-12-18}}</ref> in 2000<ref>{{harvnb|Källersjö|Bergqvist|Anderberg|2000}}</ref> and finally, in 2009 with the introduction of the [[APG III system]], was returned to the family Primulaceae, in the subfamily [[Myrsinoideae]].<ref>{{harvnb|Stevens|2012}}</ref>

The [[Type (biology)#Lectotype|lectotype]] species is ''Cyclamen europaeum'' L., a synonym of ''Cyclamen purpurascens'' Mill.; it was designated by Hitchcock & Green, in the ''International Botanical Congress. Cambridge (England), 1930. Nomenclature. Proposals by British Botanists'': 129 (Aug. 1929).<ref>{{cite web |title=Biblioteca Digital Real Jardín Botánico Madrid RJB CSIC |website=Biblioteca Digital Real Jardín Botánico Madrid RJB CSIC |url=https://bibdigital.rjb.csic.es/viewer/13040/#page=130&viewer=picture&o=bookmark&n=0&q= |access-date=2026-07-07}}</ref>

